'''Karen Austin''' is an American [[actress]]. She played Lana Wagner on the sitcom ''[[Night Court]]'' in 1984. Her film appearances include ''[[Summer Rental]]'' (1985), ''[[Far from Home (1989 film)|Far from Home]]'' (1989), and ''[[The Rum Diary (film)|The Rum Diary]]'' (2011).

==Career==
Austin first gained notability in the late 1970s with a string of television guest appearances on highly rated programs such as ''[[Happy Days]]'', ''[[The Rockford Files]]'', ''[[CHiPs]]'', and ''[[Dallas (TV series)|Dallas]]''. In the 1980s, she was a regular on the first season of the successful NBC comedy series ''[[Night Court]]'' as [[court clerk]] Lana Wagner for the first 10 episodes (but she received credits for all 13 episodes of the first season). She was asked to leave the series due to her recently diagnosed [[Bell's palsy]] which producers believed was affecting her performance.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kundu |first=Tamal |date=2023-01-25 |title=Why Did Karen Austin Leave Night Court, Explained |url=https://thecinemaholic.com/why-did-karen-austin-leave-night-court-explained/ |access-date=2023-06-08 |website=The Cinemaholic |language=en-US}}</ref> Her character was replaced by Mac Robinson ([[Charles Robinson (actor, born 1945)|Charles Robinson]]) for the remaining eight seasons. Austin had a lead role as the wife of [[John Candy]]'s character in ''[[Summer Rental]]'' (1985).

==Personal life==
Austin was married to Kris Slava at age 19; the couple divorced seven years later.<ref name="spt">{{cite news |last1=Evertz |first1=Mary |title=Self-discipline is Karen Austin's key to film stardom |url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?nid=888&dat=19781222&id=seJYAAAAIBAJ&sjid=K3wDAAAAIBAJ&pg=6599,5316411&hl=en |access-date=June 30, 2022 |work=St. Petersburg Times |date=December 22, 1978 |page=2 D}}</ref><ref name="brn">{{cite news |last1=Sheffield |first1=Skip |title=Film a home movie for Austin |url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?nid=1291&dat=19850813&id=S_5TAAAAIBAJ&sjid=So0DAAAAIBAJ&pg=6290,3732677&hl=en |access-date=June 30, 2022 |work=Boca Raton News |date=August 13, 1985 |page=B 1}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Thompson |first1=Ruth |title=Karen Austin Tries Comedy Role In 'Night Court' |url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?nid=1356&dat=19840204&id=iGhRAAAAIBAJ&sjid=FwYEAAAAIBAJ&pg=2257,2091885&hl=en |access-date=June 30, 2022 |work=Ocala Star-Banner |agency=Newspaper Enterprise Association |date=February 4, 1984 |page=15}}</ref>

